# Container & Secrets Reviewer Rule v1.1 STRICT

**Do not inline-audit.** Invoke **`container_secrets_reviewer`** -> `.cursor/agents/container_secrets_reviewer.md`.

## References

| Artifact | Path |
|---|---|
| Policy | `.cursor/skills/container_secrets_reviewer/POLICY.md` |
| Scan skill | `.cursor/skills/container_secrets_reviewer/SKILL.md` |
| Report path | `AI/container_secrets_reviewer/container_secrets_reviewer_report.md` |
| Report line | `container_secrets_reviewer v1.1 STRICT` |

**POLICY.md wins.**

## Fleet run order

`vulnerability_reviewer` → **`container_secrets_reviewer`** (this rule, if Docker/git secrets) → `supply_chain_reviewer` (if HTML/CDN)

## Invoke when

Use before deploy or when `Dockerfile`, `.gitignore`, or `application.properties`/`yml` files defining sensitive configurations change.

Skip for generated output, `target/`, `node_modules/`, and docs-only edits unless the docs define secret handling.

## Non-negotiable rules

1. **Running a container as root (missing `USER` directive) is always FAIL (SEC02).**
2. **Hardcoded secrets or live fallbacks in properties are always FAIL (SEC09).**
3. **Missing `.env` or keystore definitions from `.gitignore` is always FAIL (SEC06, SEC07, SEC08).**
4. **Unpinned `FROM` or `:latest` base images are always FAIL (SEC01)** — formerly vulnerability V08.

## Finding table

Every finding includes:

| Row | Content |
|---|---|
| Evidence | Bad line or runtime proof from project |
| Policy Rule | POLICY.md - CHECK-ID - citation |
| Pattern | SKILL.md section 8 pattern |
| Mechanism | Plain English + framework/API names |
| Security property | What must be true after fix |
| Prohibited | Short label only |
| Verify | Action + pass signal |

Allowed verdicts: **PASS**, **FAIL**, **MANUAL_REVIEW**, **N/A**. `UNCLEAR` is forbidden.
